 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "intro",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Loop unrolling removed branches. The ones that remain still cost cycles, unless we guess their direction correctly. This short video covers the guesses made before the program runs."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "head"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Static branch prediction"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Five stages: why predict, four static schemes, the delayed branch, counting mispredictions in nested loops, and an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "stages[0..=4]"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "why",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 1: every wrong guess costs a penalty of a few cycles, while the pipeline throws away wrongly fetched instructions."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 1 of 5: why predict"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "stages"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "So the CPI is 1, plus the branch frequency, times the misprediction rate, times the penalty."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "mark",
       "target": "why[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "With 20 percent branches and a 2-cycle penalty, getting every branch wrong would raise the CPI to 1.4. Every percent of accuracy matters."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "why[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A static prediction is fixed before the program runs, by the hardware's rule or by the compiler. It never changes while running."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "reveal",
       "target": "why[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "why[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "CPI = 1 + f × miss rate × penalty"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "schemes",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 2: four static schemes."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 2 of 5: four static schemes"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "why"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "sch"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Predict not taken: keep fetching the next instruction, and flush it if the branch turns out taken. The simplest hardware, which is what our 5-stage pipeline did in Module 1."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sch[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Predict taken: start fetching from the target. Loops make most branches taken, but the target address must be known early."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sch[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "BTFN: backward taken, forward not taken. A branch jumping backward is usually a loop, so guess taken. A forward branch is usually an if, so guess not taken."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sch[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Profile-based: run the program once on sample input, record which way each branch usually went, and let the compiler mark it with a hint bit. Misprediction rates vary a lot between programs."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "sch[3]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "not taken · taken · BTFN · profile"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "delay",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 3: an older trick, the delayed branch. The instruction right after the branch, its delay slot, always runs, whatever the branch does."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 3 of 5: the delayed branch"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "sch"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "ds"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The best filler comes from before the branch, if the branch does not depend on it. Then the slot always does useful work."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ds[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Here, the branch tests R4 and the add writes R1, so the add can move into the slot."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "ds"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "dsc"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Otherwise, take one from the target, which helps when the branch is taken, or from the fall-through, which helps when it is not. Either must be harmless on the other path."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "dsc"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "ds"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ds[1]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "ds[2]",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Delayed branches suited simple 5-stage pipelines. With deep pipelines and multiple issue, one slot is not enough, so modern processors predict dynamically instead."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "delay slot: always executed · fill from before if possible"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "nested",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Stage 4: counting. Two nested loops. The outer one runs 10 times, the inner one 4 times per outer iteration. Each loop's branch sits at its bottom, jumping backward."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Stage 4 of 5: counting mispredictions"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "ds"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "nl"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "nlt"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The inner branch runs 4 times per outer pass: taken 3 times, then not taken once, to exit. Over 10 passes: taken 30 times, not taken 10."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "goto_line",
       "target": "nl",
       "line": 4
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "nlt[0][1]",
       "value": "30"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "nlt[0][2]",
       "value": "10",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The outer branch runs 10 times: taken 9 times, not taken once."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "goto_line",
       "target": "nl",
       "line": 5
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "nlt[1][1]",
       "value": "9"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "nlt[1][2]",
       "value": "1",
       "delay": 0.4
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "In total, 50 branch executions: 39 taken, 11 not taken."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "nlt[2][1]",
       "value": "39"
      },
      {
       "action": "set",
       "target": "nlt[2][2]",
       "value": "11",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "nlt[2]",
       "delay": 0.5
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Predict not taken is wrong on every taken branch: 39 of 50, 78 percent. The CPI becomes 1.31."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "nl"
      },
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "nlt"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "nlm"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "nlm[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Predict taken is wrong only on the 11 exits: 22 percent, a CPI of 1.09."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "nlm[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "And BTFN gives the same here, since both branches jump backward. It differs only when forward branches appear, as in the exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "nlm[2]"
      },
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "loop branch: wrong once per loop exit when predicted taken"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "exam",
   "steps": [
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Now an exam question."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "head",
       "text": "Exam question"
      },
