     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "A loop of 100 iterations with its branch at the bottom. Inside, a forward if-branch, taken 30 times. 25 percent of instructions are branches, and a misprediction costs 3 cycles. Find the mispredictions, the rates, and the CPI under not taken, taken, and BTFN. Pause and work it out."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "q[0]"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "q[1]",
       "delay": 0.3
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "q[2]",
       "delay": 0.6
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Not taken: wrong on the 99 loop-backs and on the 30 taken ifs. 129 of 200 branches, 64.5 percent. CPI: 1 plus 0.25 times 0.645 times 3, about 1.48."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "hide",
       "target": "q"
      },
      {
       "action": "show",
       "target": "qa"
      },
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "qa[0]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "Taken: wrong on the one loop exit, and on the 70 untaken ifs. 71, 35.5 percent, CPI about 1.27."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "qa[1]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "BTFN: the backward loop branch is guessed taken, wrong once. The forward if is guessed not taken, wrong 30 times. 31, 15.5 percent, CPI about 1.12. The best of the three."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "highlight",
       "target": "qa[2]"
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "say": {
      "en": "The usual slip: forgetting that a loop branch is not taken once, at the exit."
     },
     "do": [
      {
       "action": "write",
       "target": "takeaway"
      },
      {
       "action": "replace",
       "target": "takeaway",
       "text": "BTFN wins when loops and ifs mix"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
